    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. I'll improve understandability by:\n- Removing the five unused constants (none appear in the actual test)\n- Adding a clear Javadoc to the test method explaining what it verifies\n- Adding brief inline comments to the helper methods so the control flow is obvious\n- Renaming the silent `effectiveEncoding` logic to be self-documentingThe improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed five unused constants (`TEXT_LATIN1`, `TEXT_LATIN7`, `TEXT_LATIN15`, `TEXT_EUC_JP`, `TEXT_UNICODE`), added Javadocs to all methods explaining their purpose and the assertions they perform, replaced the ternary-chained `effectiveEncoding` assignment with a clear if/else-if/else block with a descriptive variable name `resolvedEncoding`, and reordered `checkXmlWriter` overloads so the full-parameter version comes first."
    }
